# The tracker's working state, all of it. Never a list of individual files: this used to name
# `.ps/session`, `.ps/cookies*` and `.ps/catalog.json`, so every state file added afterwards —
# the watch token, the timers, the backup marker, the whole raw-frame queue — was committed
# by default, and one of those is a credential (#122). A list that has to be extended every
# time the server learns to write something is a list that will be wrong.
#
# Nothing under here belongs in a repository you push. The records do; this is how they were
# made.
.ps/

# The tracker's exclusive lock on this repository. It normally lives inside .git/, where git
# cannot see it; this covers the one case where it cannot — a run from before `git init`.
.programmers-tracker.lock

# OS
.DS_Store
